\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 5. Scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Seeking feedback
\f0\b0 \
"What's one thing I could have done better in [situation]? I'd genuinely like to hear it." For a trusted colleague: "I'm working on being more open to feedback, especially the kind that's a little uncomfortable to give. Is there something from the last month you've hesitated to bring up?"\

\f1\b Pausing before a reactive decision
\f0\b0 \
To yourself: "I don't need to answer this right now. I'll take [an hour / until tomorrow] to think through who else this affects." To someone pressing for an answer: "This matters enough that I want to get it right rather than fast \'97 let me come back to you by [specific time]."\

\f1\b Giving credit
\f0\b0 \
In a meeting: "Before I go further \'97 this happened because [Name] did [specific thing]. I want that on the record." In writing: "Quick shout-out: [Name]'s work on [X] made this possible \'97 wanted to make sure that's visible."\

\f1\b Repairing harm
\f0\b0 \
"I've been thinking about [situation], and I don't think I handled it well \'97 specifically, I [name the action]. I can see how that landed on you, and I'm sorry. Here's what I'll do differently: [specific change]."\

\f1\b Responding ethically to conflict
\f0\b0 \
"We clearly see this differently. Before we land anywhere, can we each lay out what a fair outcome looks like, and why?" "Let's separate what's easiest from what's actually fair here \'97 even if the fair option costs us more right now."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 6. Questions to ask yourself before applying any of this\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Does my workplace culture support open discussion of decision trade-offs, or could more transparency here conflict with legitimate confidentiality (HR, legal, competitive) needs?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Do I have enough psychological safety with this specific person to ask for candid feedback, or would it put them in an awkward spot given our power difference?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Would naming this colleague's contribution publicly feel supportive to them, or could it draw unwanted attention to someone who prefers to work quietly?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Is this the right moment for a repair conversation, or would it land better with a little more time, or a more private setting?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Am I doing this because it will genuinely help the relationship, or because it will make me look like I'm improving?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Is there someone whose feedback about me I've been systematically avoiding \'97 and why?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 7. A final, important caveat\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Hold these results loosely. Self-report questionnaires like this are a useful mirror, not a verdict \'97 they're shaped by your mood, your self-perception, and how you read each item, and they say nothing definitive about who you are as a person. If you want a fuller picture, structured feedback from people who actually work with you will tell you more than any self-assessment can, and a qualified executive coach or organizational psychologist is the right resource for anything higher-stakes, like a promotion decision or a formal concern.\
The same caution applies even more to other people. It can be tempting to start reading this framework onto colleagues or your manager ("they're clearly high-Machiavellian"). Resist that: you don't have their consent or their data, informal diagnosis of coworkers is unreliable, and it risks treating a real person as a trait profile rather than a whole person. Keep this tool pointed at your own growth, and extend to others the same privacy and good faith you'd want applied to you.\
Happy to go deeper on any one piece \'97 role-playing a specific script, or adapting the plan around a trigger situation you're actually facing.\
